          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %strong cotangent complex
            is a
            %em derived
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-categorical
            refinement of the notion of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
          %p
            Traditionally this has been conceived in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentations. This we discuss in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ModCat"}> Model category presentation
              \.
          %p
            From the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            projection. This we discuss in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#InfCat"} (∞,1)-Categorical description
          %h3#motivation Motivation
          %p
            The construction of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transversal+map"} transversality
            of intersections when trying to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represent
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            of assigning families of objects to the varying base of family. When passing to the classes of equivalent objects, one faces the problem of having nontrivial
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
          %p
            At the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            level
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            of relative
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived
            replacement is the
            %strong cotangent complex
            of Grothendieck-Illusie. One can typically split the information about a map of higher rings into its “discrete part” and infinitesimal obstruction theory governed by the cotangent complex.
          %h2#ModCat Model category presentation
          %h3#LeftDerivedFunctorOfKaehlerDifferentials Quillen’s definition: left derived functor of Kähler differentials
          %p
            The
            %strong cotangent complex
            functor is effectively the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            of the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
          %p
            To talk about the nonabelian derived functors, Quillen introduced a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} model structure on the category of simplicial commutative rings
          %p
            Given a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A\to B
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            an
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+category"} tangent category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AbGr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AbGr(A Alg/B)
            of abelian group objects in the slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Alg/B
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is equivalent both to the category of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            by
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            In particular we can consider the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi AbGr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AbGr(A Alg/B)\to A Alg/B
            which has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi Ab
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi AbGr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{A/B} Ab_{B/A} : A Alg/B\to AbGr(A Alg/B)\cong {}_B Mod
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
          %p
            All said is true for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial commutative rings
            as well.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong relative cotangent complex
              functor is the left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi s
                    %mi A
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi s
                    %mi AbGr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi s
                    %mi B
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{L} \Omega_{B/A} :
                    s A Alg/B\to s AbGr(A Alg/B)\cong s B Mod
            %p
              Its value on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is the relative cotangent complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{B/A}
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+cohomology"} André-Quillen cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{L}\Omega(R)
          %h3#explicit_resolutions Explicit resolutions
          %p
            Here is one way to compute the required cofibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            for the construction of the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            for the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = k
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi CAlg
                  %mo →
                  %mi CAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : CAlg \to CAlg
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi CAlg
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                  %mo :
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U : CAlg \to Set : k[-]
          %p
            that sends a commutative
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            to the polynomial algebra on its underlying set.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mo •
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet R
            be the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+construction"} bar construction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mo •
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet R \to R
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            on the right regarded as a constant simplicial object is a resolution of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            Forming degreewise the module of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{k}(P_\bullet R)
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_\bullet R
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The cotangent complex of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi P
                          %mo •
                        %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{L} \Omega_{/k}) (R) \simeq
                    R \otimes_{P_\bullet R} \Omega_k(P_\bullet R)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Notice that the universal property of the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a ring and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              an
              = succeed "-module," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(\Omega(R), N) \simeq Der(R,N)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Accordingly, it follows that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+cohomology"} André-Quillen cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with values in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom((\mathbb{L}\Omega)(R), N)
            %p is equivalently the cohomology of the object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi P
                                  %mo •
                                %mi R
                            %msub
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi P
                              %mo •
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi P
                                  %mo •
                                %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi P
                              %mo •
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Der
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi P
                              %mo •
                            %mi R
                            %mo ,
                            %mi N
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\cdots &amp; \simeq
                    Hom(R \otimes_{P_\bullet R} \Omega_k(P_\bullet R), N)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{P_\bullet R}( \Omega_k(P_\bullet R), N)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Der(P_\bullet R, N)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p In particular we have the the degree-0 cohomology of this complex is the module of ordinary derivations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mo •
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Der
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^0(Der(P_\bullet R, N)) \simeq Der(R,N)
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If in the above
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of characteristic 0, then
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+cohomology"} André-Quillen cohomology
              of the
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              with coefficients in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a
              = succeed "mand" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi HH
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^q(Hom(\mathbb{L} \Omega (R)), N)
                    \\simeq
                    HH^{q+1}_{(1)}(R,N)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the subscript refers to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+decomposition"} Hodge decomposition
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
          %p This is in section 8.8 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An+Introduction+to+Homological+Algebra"} An Introduction to Homological Algebra
          %h2#InfCat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-categorical description
          %p
            The
            %em cotangent complex
            is a generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            in the sense of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
          %p
            Recall from above that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            the ordinary category of commutative rings, the cotangent complex functor is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi K
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega_K : Ring \to Mod
          %p
            of the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to Ring
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differential"} Kähler differential
          %p
            This generalizes to the case where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
            is replaced by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega : C \to T_C
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dom
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dom : T_C \to C
          %p
            In particular, when
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = ...
          %h2#further_properties_and_applications Further properties and applications
          %h3#characterization_via_universal_properties Characterization via universal properties
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+complex+in+derived+geometry"} cotangent complex in derived geometry
          %h3#application_lifting_properties_of_classical_rings_to_derived_rings Application: lifting properties of classical rings to derived rings
          %p
            For more background see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
          %p
            Apart from simplicial rings we can consider
            = succeed "-rings." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            = succeed "-rings" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            plus a condition on the relative cotangent complex. Similarly, one can express the descent properties of higher stacks via the usual gluing at the bottom level plus the obstruction theory for relative cotangent complex. Study of an appropriate version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Postnikov+tower"} Postnikov tower
            is a systematic way to do this.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"}> deformation theory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+deformation+theory"} derived deformation theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+complex"}> tangent complex
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+cohomology"} André-Quillen cohomology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %strong> cotangent complex
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+homology"} André-Quillen homology
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+homology"} Hochschild homology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Andr%C3%A9-Quillen+homology"}> topological André-Quillen homology
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+Hochschild+homology"} topological Hochschild homology
          %h2#references References
          %p
            See also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            and references therein.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories cofibrées additives et complexe cotangent relatif
                %strong 79
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luc+Illusie"}> Luc Illusie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Complexe cotangent et déformations I
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 239
                = succeed "," do
                  %em II
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 283
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Behrend"}> Kai Behrend
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barbara+Fantechi"} Barbara Fantechi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The intrinsic normal cone
                %strong 128
                (1997), no. 1, 45–88, MR1437495 (98e:14022)
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9601010"} arXiv:alg-geom/9601010
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barbara+Fantechi"}> Barbara Fantechi
                , M. Manetti,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Obstruction calculus for functors of Artin rings I
                %strong 202
                (1998), no. 2, 541–576, MR1617687 (99f:14004).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deformation+Theory"} Deformation Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.3091"} arXiv:0709.3091
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spectra in model categories and applications to the algebraic cotangent complex
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 120
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(96)00058-8"} doi
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Weibel"}> Charles Weibel
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An+Introduction+to+Homological+Algebra"} An Introduction to Homological Algebra
                section 8.8.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"}> Gabriele Vezzosi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A note on the cotangent complex in derived algebraic geometry
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1008.0601"} arxiv/1008.0601
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Stacks+Project"}> The Stacks Project
                ,
                %em The cotangent complex
                (
                %a{:href => "http://stacks.math.columbia.edu/download/cotangent.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            A short exposition (from the point of view of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+schemes"} formal schemes
          %ul
            %li
              chapter 5 (5.29-5.31) in Luc Illusie,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck’s existence theorem in formal geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA+explained"} FGA explained
              (179–233) MR2223409; (draft version
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://cdsagenda5.ictp.it//askArchive.php?categ=a0255&id=a0255s3t3&ifd=15021&down=1&type=lecture_notes"} pdf
          %p
            The cotangent complex for a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra over an operad
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            is discussed in section 7 of
          %ul
            %li#Hinich
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              %em Homological algebra of homotopy algebras
              Communications in algebra, 25(10). 3291-3323 (1997)(
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702015"}> arXiv:q-alg/9702015
              ,
              %em Erratum
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309453"}> arXiv:math/0309453
              ))
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentations for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} tangent (infinity,1)-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yonatan+Harpaz"}> Yonatan Harpaz
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"} Joost Nuiten
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matan+Prasma"} Matan Prasma
                %em Tangent categories of algebras over operads
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.02607"}> arXiv:1612.02607
                )
            %li
              %p
                %em The abstract cotangent complex and Quillen cohomology of enriched categories
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.02608"}> arXiv:1612.02608
                )
